00:22:13.616 --> 00:22:16.552
- Your present or past results have

00:22:16.552 --> 00:22:19.283
absolutely nothing to do

00:22:19.283 --> 00:22:22.420
with what's going to happen
from this point forward.

00:22:22.420 --> 00:22:25.536
Now that was the point that Ray Stanford

00:22:25.536 --> 00:22:27.037
drilled into my head.

00:22:27.037 --> 00:22:29.783
You see I kept thinking,
well gee I such a mess up

00:22:29.783 --> 00:22:32.988
you know I've done
everything wrong up 'til now.

00:22:32.988 --> 00:22:35.437
I'm 26, I'm broke, I'm not happy.

00:22:35.437 --> 00:22:36.899
Everything was wrong.

00:22:36.899 --> 00:22:39.982
He said, "Bob that's all in the past.

00:22:41.903 --> 00:22:45.153
He said, "Every moment is a new moment.

00:22:47.933 --> 00:22:51.116
"We shouldn't condemn ourselves.

00:22:51.116 --> 00:22:54.504
And he said, "What you were
yesterday you paid for.

00:22:54.504 --> 00:22:57.257
"What you are today you decide what."

00:22:57.257 --> 00:22:59.949
That's exactly what Troy would say.

00:22:59.949 --> 00:23:03.699
This power in no way is
limited by precedent.

00:23:05.822 --> 00:23:08.421
Even in a creative
state we sometimes don't

00:23:08.421 --> 00:23:10.402
understand that.

00:23:10.402 --> 00:23:12.954
You know why airplanes right up to today

00:23:12.954 --> 00:23:15.189
almost have wings on them?

00:23:15.189 --> 00:23:17.272
Because birds have wings.

00:23:18.531 --> 00:23:19.999
Birds fly.

00:23:19.999 --> 00:23:21.666
They have wings.

00:23:21.666 --> 00:23:23.326
If you're going to get a plane to fly

00:23:23.326 --> 00:23:24.574
you've got to put wings on it.

00:23:24.574 --> 00:23:27.524
Do you, no, we've got planes
flying without wings today.

00:23:27.524 --> 00:23:29.465
You know why, never didn't need wings.

00:23:29.465 --> 00:23:32.115
But you see the thinking
was to a degree limited

00:23:32.115 --> 00:23:33.491
by precedent.

00:23:33.491 --> 00:23:35.497
Birds fly with wings
planes have to have wings.

00:23:35.497 --> 00:23:38.929
Planes do not have to have wings.

00:23:38.929 --> 00:23:41.191
You're creative if you can
visualize it you can do it.

00:23:41.191 --> 00:23:42.922
It doesn't matter what it
is, that's what Hill said

00:23:42.922 --> 00:23:44.282
anything the mind can
conceive and believe it

00:23:44.282 --> 00:23:45.519
you can achieve.

00:23:45.519 --> 00:23:49.237
You see the beautiful part
about goals and understanding it

00:23:49.237 --> 00:23:51.322
is goals are not to get.

00:23:51.322 --> 00:23:54.572
Goals is not you don't
set goals for acquisition.

00:23:54.572 --> 00:23:56.405
You set goals to grow.

00:23:57.335 --> 00:24:00.639
You set goals to reach inside and stretch

00:24:00.639 --> 00:24:02.807
and go where you've never been.

00:24:02.807 --> 00:24:05.246
You set goals to take into a place

00:24:05.246 --> 00:24:07.167
you've never gone before.

00:24:07.167 --> 00:24:09.204
And you grow as your human
being and you know something

00:24:09.204 --> 00:24:10.666
you never go back.

00:24:10.666 --> 00:24:13.284
Choice is one of the
most important concepts

00:24:13.284 --> 00:24:14.240
that you can get.

00:24:14.240 --> 00:24:15.855
We're going to be talking about

00:24:15.855 --> 00:24:16.935
the laws of the universe.

00:24:16.935 --> 00:24:18.891
One of the laws is a law clarity.

00:24:18.891 --> 00:24:20.767
There'd be note inside
to the room you're in

00:24:20.767 --> 00:24:22.096
if there was an outside.

00:24:22.096 --> 00:24:23.607
You couldn't have a right side your body

00:24:23.607 --> 00:24:25.450
without a left or a top or a bottom.

00:24:25.450 --> 00:24:26.831
Or a front without a back.

00:24:26.831 --> 00:24:28.928
You can't have a bad without a good.

00:24:28.928 --> 00:24:32.700
See the truth is we make it bad or good.

00:24:32.700 --> 00:24:34.843
Ralph Waldo Trin

00:24:34.843 --> 00:24:37.429
In Tune With The Infinite, a great book.

00:24:37.429 --> 00:24:40.602
He said, "Nothing is
good or bad except our

00:24:40.602 --> 00:24:42.029
"will make it so."

00:24:42.029 --> 00:24:44.213
Well if everything is both good and bad

00:24:44.213 --> 00:24:45.596
and we bring it together what's right

00:24:45.596 --> 00:24:46.742
in the center?

00:24:46.742 --> 00:24:50.155
If everything here is bad
everything here is good,

00:24:50.155 --> 00:24:51.158
what's in the center?

00:24:51.158 --> 00:24:52.817
Just is.

00:24:52.817 --> 00:24:54.400
Everything just is.

00:24:55.886 --> 00:24:58.735
You choose whether you're going to look at

00:24:58.735 --> 00:25:00.591
the downside or the upside.

00:25:00.591 --> 00:25:03.125
Michael Beckwith gave
me a marvelous concept,

00:25:03.125 --> 00:25:05.878
he said, "It doesn't matter
what happens in your life

00:25:05.878 --> 00:25:07.924
"doesn't matter what happens
you can't control the

00:25:07.924 --> 00:25:09.979
"circumstance but you
can certainly control

00:25:09.979 --> 00:25:11.534
"how you deal with them."

00:25:11.534 --> 00:25:14.718
He said, "When anything happens

00:25:14.718 --> 00:25:18.139
"step number one it is
what it is accept it.

00:25:18.139 --> 00:25:20.160
"It's either going to control you

00:25:20.160 --> 00:25:21.891
"or you're going to control it."

00:25:21.891 --> 00:25:22.762
That's a choice.

00:25:22.762 --> 00:25:25.318
Step number two, "Harvest the good."

00:25:25.318 --> 00:25:27.012
Isn't that a neat word, harvest?

00:25:27.012 --> 00:25:29.073
Harvest the good.

00:25:29.073 --> 00:25:30.217
There's good and bad in everything

00:25:30.217 --> 00:25:31.456
just harvest the good.

00:25:31.456 --> 00:25:34.797
Step number three, "Forgive all the rest."

00:25:34.797 --> 00:25:37.684
Forgive means like go up completely.

00:25:37.684 --> 00:25:38.851
It's a choice.

00:25:39.815 --> 00:25:41.296
Yet if you let go of the bad

00:25:41.296 --> 00:25:43.029
the good seems to grow.

00:25:43.029 --> 00:25:44.695
You and I have a choice.

00:25:44.695 --> 00:25:46.394
It may be a difficult choice

00:25:46.394 --> 00:25:48.553
sometimes if you're
dealing with a particular

00:25:48.553 --> 00:25:50.118
difficult individual

00:25:50.118 --> 00:25:52.397
or a particularly difficult circumstance.

00:25:52.397 --> 00:25:56.543
Nevertheless we've got the
power within us to do it.

00:25:56.543 --> 00:25:59.328
So as you go through the
day doesn't matter what

00:25:59.328 --> 00:26:01.620
anybody says doesn't matter what happens

00:26:01.620 --> 00:26:04.230
you have a choice to say,

00:26:04.230 --> 00:26:05.696
"That's good."

00:26:05.696 --> 00:26:09.016
W Clement Stone became the wealthiest man

00:26:09.016 --> 00:26:12.128
in the United States of America by 1970

00:26:12.128 --> 00:26:14.006
because he always said,

00:26:14.006 --> 00:26:14.892
"That's good."

00:26:14.892 --> 00:26:17.406
Doesn't matter what it was
he'd say, "That's good."

00:26:17.406 --> 00:26:19.232
And then he'd look for the good.

00:26:19.232 --> 00:26:21.124
That's a good choice for you to make

00:26:21.124 --> 00:26:23.235
and make it all day long.

00:26:23.235 --> 00:26:26.005
So your word for the day
is choice, choice, choice.

00:26:26.005 --> 00:26:29.457
And only you have the ability to do that.

00:26:29.457 --> 00:26:31.268
And if you choose right

00:26:31.268 --> 00:26:34.601
you are going to get results that stick.

